wsi: swapchain images in AHardwareBuffers from the DroidNux display server

With DROIDNUX_AHB_SOCKET set, native DRM images of BGRA swapchains are
imported from buffers the app allocates (one connection per buffer, see
display/src/main/cpp/core/allocator.h), with an explicit linear layout at
the buffer's row pitch. The display server recognizes them when they come
back through DRI3 and hands full-screen ones to Android's compositor as
they are. Rows are added when the driver pads the image.

